====================================================================================================
PART 2. DO EFFECTS REALLY DIFFER ACROSS COUNTRIES? (service level, listings)
====================================================================================================

--- listings: 11 countries with a one-year estimate ---
  a) Cochran's Q = 34.4 on 10 df, p = 0.000; I-squared = 71%  (generous to finding differences: ignores country-specific shocks)
  b) Spread of country estimates AFTER (one year) = 1.03 points; BEFORE (placebo) = 0.47 points (11 countries).
     Variance ratio after/before = 4.88, one-sided p = 0.010; Levene test p = 0.078
     If the spread after is not clearly larger than before, the variation is no more than country noise.
  c) Each listed country's own one-year estimate (95% interval treats its services as independent,
     so it is too narrow if country-specific shocks matter):
     Botswana           +2.02  (+0.52 to +3.52); services 7
     South Africa       +1.42  (+0.78 to +2.07); services 46
     Uganda             +1.33  (+0.43 to +2.24); services 28
     Tunisia            +0.56  (-0.09 to +1.22); services 24
     South Sudan        +0.12  (-1.59 to +1.82); services 22
     Cameroon           +0.04  (-0.61 to +0.69); services 29
     Senegal            -0.01  (-2.13 to +2.10); services 8
     Cote d'Ivoire      -0.02  (-0.95 to +0.92); services 13
     Mali               -0.60  (-1.60 to +0.41); services 9
     Congo, Dem. Rep.   -0.97  (-2.10 to +0.15); services 20
     Mozambique         -1.29  (-2.91 to +0.33); services 21

--- all changes, removals sign-reversed: 17 countries with a one-year estimate ---
  a) Cochran's Q = 38.7 on 16 df, p = 0.001; I-squared = 59%  (generous to finding differences: ignores country-specific shocks)
  b) Spread of country estimates AFTER (one year) = 1.03 points; BEFORE (placebo) = 0.56 points (20 countries).
     Variance ratio after/before = 3.36, one-sided p = 0.007; Levene test p = 0.019
     If the spread after is not clearly larger than before, the variation is no more than country noise.

